+{
+ "cells": [
+  {
+   "cell_type": "raw",
+   "id": "perc-intro",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "The `Perc` stat replaces observations with percentile values. It returns one row for each requested percentile within each group, with the percentile level recorded in a `percentile` column. The default `k=5` produces the endpoints and default quartiles (0, 25, 50, 75, and 100). Integer values of `k` request that many evenly spaced levels from 0 to 100, inclusive; a list supplies explicit levels. The default `method=`linear`` interpolates between observations. `method` accepts any method supported by `numpy.percentile`: `inverted_cdf`, `averaged_inverted_cdf`, `closest_observation`, `interpolated_inverted_cdf`, `hazen`, `weibull`, `linear`, `median_unbiased`, `normal_unbiased`, `lower`, `higher`, `midpoint`, and `nearest`."
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "id": "perc-setup",
+   "metadata": {"tags": ["hide"]},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "import seaborn.objects as so\n",
+    "from seaborn import load_dataset\n",
+    "penguins = load_dataset(\"penguins\")"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "raw",
+   "id": "perc-count",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": ["Request three evenly spaced levels:"]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "id": "perc-count-code",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "(\n",
+    "    so.Plot(penguins, x=\"species\", y=\"body_mass_g\")\n",
+    "    .add(so.Dot(), so.Perc(k=3))\n",
+    ")"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "raw",
+   "id": "perc-levels",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": ["Supply explicit levels, such as the quartiles and endpoints:"]
+  },
